  "body": "I’m excited to introduce an outstanding St Heliers opportunity offering an increasingly rare combination of space, views, flexibility and exceptional parking.\r\n\r\n• 320m² home on 659m² of freehold land\r\n• Four generous bedrooms\r\n• Two and a half bathrooms\r\n• Two living areas plus dining\r\n• Three-car internal-access garage + workshop\r\n• Additional off-street parking for multiple vehicles, a boat or caravan\r\n• Internal lift servicing all three levels\r\n• Elevated city, North Head and wider Auckland views\r\n• Large, warm north-facing deck\r\n• Flat, north-facing garden with separate access\r\n• Recently upgraded kitchen and interiors\r\n• Cedar, concrete block and STO cavity-system exterior construction\r\n• CV: $3,300,000\r\n\r\nPositioned high on the ridge in St Heliers, this substantial freehold residence is the end home in a boutique group of just four. Quietly set back from the road, yet moments from the best of the Bays, it offers an impressive 320m² of living across three levels — all conveniently connected by an internal lift.\r\n\r\nThe entrance level sets the tone with a striking three-storey atrium, triple-car garaging, a well-equipped workshop, excellent storage, separate laundry and lift access to the levels above.\r\n\r\nLevels two and three offer exceptional flexibility, making the home ideal for downsizers who don’t want to compromise on space, families with older children, or those wanting plenty of room for visiting guests. The middle level features three generous bedrooms, a family bathroom and light-filled living with a kitchenette opening directly to the fully fenced lawn and garden.\r\n\r\nUpstairs is the showstopper. High ceilings, expansive windows and open-plan living capture spectacular views, while the generous primary suite connects through wide cavity sliders. A powder room for guests completes this level, creating easy single-level living when it’s just the two of you at home.\r\n\r\nThe outlook is superb, stretching from the Tamaki Estuary towards the Waitakere Ranges on one side and across St Heliers towards North Head on the other, with balconies connecting you to the views from every level.\r\n\r\nWaimarie Street’s cafés, restaurants and everyday conveniences are just steps away, with Churchill Park, Glover Park, St Heliers Beach and the village all close by. Zoned for Churchill Park School and Glendowie College, with easy access to the CBD.\r\n\r\nLovingly maintained by the owners for more than 20 years, only a move out of Auckland is prompting the sale.",
